Route A plain-pointer ABI for non-PAC arm64, XNU 12377.121.6.

Apply after UniXNU 8542980d02b4d2cc5c32ee3542de1760b2562aac:
  patches/xnu-12377/native-4k-shared-region-slide.patch
Base XNU: ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f.

The v3/v5 whole-page and dyld-pager changes are adapted from:
  none24smu/UniXNU a8b90c0c645fd62ae850cd43e80c87bab4cc157d
  native-shared-region-plain-auth.patch
  native-dyld-pager-plain-auth.patch
Upstream adaptation copyright (c) 2026, UniXNU contributors:
BSD-2-Clause-Patent, retained at scripts/route_a_zeta/LICENSE.
Affected XNU files retain their APSL-2.0 / OSREFERENCE notices; the
project license does not replace those original file licenses.
The part-v5 no-PAC writeback and fixup_page error propagation are added
locally for the newer 4 KiB pager and the newly exposed auth fixup paths.

This selects a process-wide plain-pointer compatibility ABI. It provides
no authentication. Target code and every participating loader must agree
on that ABI. It is not a general way to run unmodified arm64e binaries.

Patch application and extracted-function host tests do not qualify a
complete kernel build, pager concurrency, or hardware boot. See
upstream/route-a-kernel-sources.json and docs/ROUTE_A_PLAIN_AUTH_PATCH.md.

